{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":492143,"name":"ziemovit","username":"ziemovit","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/z/9de053/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-15T21:05:34.588Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492143-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492143-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492143-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492143-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA Bot-owned routine with a GitHub “issue assigned” trigger never starts, even though the assignment event exists on GitHub, the Cursor GitHub App has access to the repository, and the Bot handles the same issue fine when asked in chat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSetup\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA Bot owns one routine, shown in the routine panel as: \u003cem\u003eWhen an issue is assigned in \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;my-account\u0026gt;/\u0026lt;private-repo\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e (by \u003ccode\u003e@\u0026lt;second-account\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/em\u003e, no schedule, status Active.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;second-account\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e is a separate GitHub user added as a collaborator on that private repo. A server-side job uses its token to create an issue via the REST API with \u003ccode\u003eassignees: [\"\u0026lt;my-account\u0026gt;\"]\u003c/code\u003e, plus labels.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe issue timeline confirms the event: \u003ccode\u003eassigned\u003c/code\u003e, actor \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;second-account\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e, assignee \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;my-account\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGitHub integration is connected in the Cursor dashboard as my personal account; the Cursor GitHub App is installed on that account with \u003cstrong\u003eAll repositories\u003c/strong\u003e and read/write on issues.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRelated:\u003c/strong\u003e webhook routines are not a workaround here, because of the known issue tracked in \u003ca href=\"https://forum.cursor.com/t/desktop-grok-bot-webhook-routine-shows-no-post-url-crsr-key-windows-0-47-0/171324\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eDesktop Grok Bot webhook routine shows no POST URL / crsr_ key (Windows 0.47.0)\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492143-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492143-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate the routine above from chat.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate an issue in the repo as \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;second-account\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e, assigned to \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;my-account\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait several minutes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat I tried (all times UTC, 2026-09-15)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"md-table\"\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n\u003cthead\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eIssue created and assigned\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eCondition\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003cth\u003eResult\u003c/th\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/thead\u003e\n\u003ctbody\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e19:21:44\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ebefore the Cursor GitHub App was installed\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eno run\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e19:37:55\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003ebefore the Cursor GitHub App was installed\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eno run\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e19:42:46\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eafter installing the app with All repositories\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eno run\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e19:47:15\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eafter deleting and recreating the routine\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eno run\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003ctr\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003e20:17:03\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eafter enabling on-site GitHub notifications; the “You were assigned” notification arrived in my inbox at 20:17:24\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003ctd\u003eno run\u003c/td\u003e\n\u003c/tr\u003e\n\u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRuled out:\u003c/strong\u003e repository access, since the Cursor app has All repositories and read/write on issues; routine age, since a recreated routine behaves the same; on-site notifications, since after I enabled them the assignment notification reached my GitHub inbox within about 20 seconds and the routine still did not run.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492143-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492143-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExpected:\u003c/strong\u003e the routine runs and the Bot handles the issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eActual:\u003c/strong\u003e no run in the routine history and no activity in the Bot’s chat. Asking the Bot in chat to handle the same issue works fine, so the Bot, its GitHub tools and the repo access are OK. Only the event trigger is silent.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492143-operating-system-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492143-operating-system-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492143-version-information-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492143-version-information-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot:\u003cbr\u003e\nVersion: 0.51.0\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: darwin (macOS 26.6.2, Apple Silicon)\u003cbr\u003e\nPlan: SuperGrok, Privacy Mode on\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492143-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492143-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQuestions\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eShould an \u003ccode\u003eissue assigned\u003c/code\u003e routine fire when a different collaborator account creates the issue with the assignee already set, rather than assigning it afterwards?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDoes the trigger listen for a specific webhook event, for example \u003ccode\u003eissues.assigned\u003c/code\u003e rather than \u003ccode\u003eissues.opened\u003c/code\u003e carrying assignees, and does the “(by \u003cspan class=\"mention\"\u003e@user\u003c/span\u003e)” filter compare the assigner, the issue author, or the assignee?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIs there a way to see received or unmatched events for a routine, to tell “not delivered” from “delivered but filtered”?\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks. I can share exact timestamps or routine IDs privately with the team.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-492143-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-492143-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T06:00:17.597Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":13,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":66.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171791,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-github-issue-assigned-routine-never-fires-5-attempts-recreated-routine-app-has-repo-access","display_username":"ziemovit","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/desktop-grok-bot-webhook-routine-shows-no-post-url-crsr-key-windows-0-47-0/171324","internal":true,"reflection":false,"title":"Desktop Grok Bot webhook routine shows no POST URL / crsr_ key (Windows 0.47.0)","clicks":0},{"url":"https://forum.cursor.com/t/desktop-grok-bot-webhook-routine-shows-no-post-url-crsr-key-windows-0-47-0/171324/28","internal":true,"reflection":true,"title":"Desktop Grok Bot webhook routine shows no POST URL / crsr_ key (Windows 0.47.0)","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":137967,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-github-issue-assigned-routine-never-fires-5-attempts-recreated-routine-app-has-repo-access/171791/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":492316,"name":"Dean Rie","username":"deanrie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-16T05:59:58.162Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey, thanks for the detailed report. Extra thanks for the timings table and for checking access, the routine itself, and notifications upfront.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMain point first: your setup is correct. This isn’t a configuration issue on your side. It’s a known issue on our side that we’re already tracking. The GitHub issue assigned trigger currently doesn’t fire for \u003ca href=\"http://github.com\"\u003egithub.com\u003c/a\u003e repositories, so the routine won’t start no matter how the assignee is set. Your access, routine, and filter are fine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn your questions:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYes, by design the routine should also trigger when a collaborator creates an issue with an assignee set right away. In that case GitHub sends a separate assigned event.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe trigger listens specifically to the assignment event assigned. The filter (by \u003cspan class=\"mention\"\u003e@user\u003c/span\u003e) checks who assigned it (the assigner), not the author or the assignee. In your case the collaborator is both the creator and the assigner, so the setup matches.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThere’s currently no user-facing log of received or non-matching routine events. Agree it would be useful, I’ve passed this on as feedback.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTemporary workaround: since webhook-routine doesn’t work for you due to 171324, the most reliable option right now is a scheduled routine. For example, every 15 minutes on weekdays, have the Bot check the repo for open issues assigned to you that it hasn’t processed yet, then handle them. If you prefer, a Slack trigger also works.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI can’t share an ETA for the event trigger fix yet, but I’ll post an update here when I have one.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-16T05:59:58.162Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":0.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":171791,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-github-issue-assigned-routine-never-fires-5-attempts-recreated-routine-app-has-repo-access","display_username":"Dean Rie","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"http://github.com","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"GitHub · Change is constant. GitHub keeps you ahead. · GitHub","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":750,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-github-issue-assigned-routine-never-fires-5-attempts-recreated-routine-app-has-repo-access/171791/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null}],"stream":[492143,492316]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,1]],"suggested_topics":[],"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":314,"name":"github","slug":"github"},{"id":376,"name":"automations","slug":"automations"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"fancy_title":"Grok Bot: GitHub \u0026ldquo;issue assigned\u0026rdquo; routine never fires (5 attempts, recreated routine, app has repo access)","id":171791,"title":"Grok Bot: GitHub \"issue assigned\" routine never fires (5 attempts, recreated routine, app has repo access)","posts_count":2,"created_at":"2026-09-15T21:05:34.559Z","views":33,"reply_count":0,"like_count":0,"last_posted_at":"2026-09-16T05:59:58.162Z","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"has_summary":false,"archetype":"regular","slug":"grok-bot-github-issue-assigned-routine-never-fires-5-attempts-recreated-routine-app-has-repo-access","category_id":6,"word_count":822,"deleted_at":null,"user_id":